# Every text file checks out with LF, whatever core.autocrlf says: the
# guard tests parse source files line by line (the notices, the built-in
# and purpose assets, the redaction kinds), and gofmt writes LF. A Windows
# checkout with autocrlf on gave them CRLF and four went red (#1827).
# internal/agent/testdata/.gitattributes keeps its real CRLF bytes.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Keep binary asset contents in Git LFS; Git history stores only pointers.
*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
